25,2,1,talk,Minato,,"Our developers are busy until the third quarter, and the coordination group is severely understaffed.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Customer plant network coverage is very spotty, and visitor device approval is a slow, bureaucratic nightmare.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,George,,"The capital budget is frozen, but we have some room in the recurring software allowance.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,May,,"Tools requiring daily entry from everyone tend to fail, while narrow, trade-specific tools survive.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Midori,,"We are losing an hour a day to copying records, and misrouted deliveries are happening because of duplicate addresses.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@George, if the capital budget is frozen, does that mean we can only do small things?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, those duplicate addresses sound like a data management problem.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,George,,"@Minato, it means we should favor recurring software costs over large one-time capital spends.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,May,,"@Midori, the time lost to copying records is exactly the kind of ""everyday loss"" we should target.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, yes, it seems we have the same information stored in different places.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@May, if tools that need everyone to use them fail, we should be careful.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I'm also worried about any project that requires technicians to use devices at customer sites.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,George,,"@George, I'll keep in mind that fixed-fee work is more stable than per-head licensing.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, that's a very important point about the network. It could kill a project.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Midori,,I agree. We need something that solves the record-copying without adding more manual work.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
